      "message": "could we centralize final-response framing in small inline helper shared by all http versions? Preserve msg.data.body_len as metadata and derive actual body presence, streaming, and Content-Length emission separately from the method and status. in particular, HTTP_MSG_DATA_STREAMING on HEAD response means unknown representation length, with no body or EOF wait. HEAD 304 without Content-Length should therefore complete after headers instead of hitting the generic streaming-status rejection. this would remove duplicated checks and the HTTP/1 mutation of body_len, keeping metadata and payload accounting explicit.\nhttp2.c:1312\nhttp3.c:601",
